# graphify

`graphify-out/` is **present on this machine**. It is gitignored (`graphify-out/` in `.gitignore`) and rebuilt by a local post-commit hook (`graphify hook install` after a fresh clone). The graph is the first place to look for codebase / architecture questions.

- **Do not use Glob, Grep, or other workspace search to decide whether it exists.** Those tools skip gitignored paths and will report a miss. Check with the shell: `test -f graphify-out/graph.json` or `ls graphify-out`.
- If `graphify-out/graph.json` is there, **query it** (`graphify query "..."`) instead of rebuilding. Do not run a full `/graphify .` unless asked.
- The hook covers **code** only. After doc or image changes, run `/graphify . --update`.
- After a fresh clone, `graphify-out/` will be empty until the hook has run or someone builds it.
